The `sed '/^$/q'` trick reads lines until the first blank line and
stops. MERGE_MSG looks like:

  Merge tag 'v1.415.0' into investigate-infeasibilities-clean

  # Conflicts:
  #	core/.../ChargersSchedule.java

So the sed command captures the subject and the blank that follows,
then exits. The blank matters: without it the appended summary runs
directly into the subject, which git reads as a continuation of the
subject line rather than the start of the body.

The eval harness that surfaced these issues runs three real merge
scenarios from investigate-infeasibilities-clean (v1.415.0, v1.415.5,
v1.415.6). With-skill: 7/7 on all three. Without-skill: 2/7, with
the merged-by trailer and the # Conflicts: block as the two regressions
this patch targets.
